% A module named after a bundled library, importing that library.
%
% Module identity is the name alone, so this module *is* `lists` for
% everything downstream and the bundled one is dropped: the import can
% never bring anything into scope. Rejected rather than left to surface
% as a library that mysteriously exports nothing.
:- module(lists, [go/1]).

:- use_module(library(lists)).

:- chr_constraint go/1.

go(R) <=> R is length([1, 2, 3]).
